# JAYSTARBLISS STUDIOS V3 — MASTER IMPLEMENTATION VERIFICATION, COMPLETION & REPAIR CHECKLIST

## OBJECTIVE

Conduct a comprehensive implementation audit of the existing Jaystarbliss Studios V3 platform against the requirements in the two previous implementation briefs:

1. **Programme Discovery, Hierarchy, Enrolment, Admissions, Student Billing, Social Sharing & Portal Onboarding.**
2. **Subscription Guardrails, Seven-Day Grace Period, Portal Lockdown, Payment Renewals, Tutor Class Links & Test Financial Data Reset.**

Your responsibility is to determine whether every requested feature has actually been implemented and works correctly.

**This is not a request to generate another plan or merely review the code. It is an audit-and-repair task.**

You must:

- Inspect the existing codebase.
- Inspect the actual Firebase data structures and rules where accessible.
- Trace complete user journeys.
- Verify both frontend and backend implementations.
- Test the relevant workflows.
- Identify every missing, incomplete, broken, insecure or incorrectly implemented requirement.
- Fix each issue you can safely resolve within the existing architecture.
- Run the appropriate tests and verify your fixes.
- Produce a final implementation report.

Do not assume a feature is complete just because a button, page, tab, database field or visual component exists.

A feature counts as complete only when its actual functionality, data flow, permissions, error handling and relevant user experience work as required.

